\Prototype architecture

Hypersphere.dm
      │
      ▼
  DM Parser
      │
      ▼
   DM AST
      │
      ▼
Dimension Engine
      │
      ├── Geometry
      ├── Topology
      ├── Fields
      └── Transformations
      │
      ▼
Observation Engine
      │
      ▼
Projection Engine
      │
      ▼
3D Renderer

The first executable object will support:

* 4D hypersphere definition
* arbitrary radius
* w-axis slicing
* 4D → 3D projection
* movement through the w dimension
* 4D rotation in the x-w plane
* interactive visualization
* .dm file loading

The canonical mathematical object is:

x^2+y^2+z^2+w^2=R^2

with a 3D slice:

x^2+y^2+z^2=R^2-w^2

and therefore:

r(w)=\sqrt{R^2-w^2}.

I can build this as an actual ￼ downloadable prototype project next, including Hypersphere.dm, the parser, renderer, and a README explaining the .dm syntax.
